 "docs.scopes": "Scopes",
 "docs.scopesBody": "Every endpoint needs one scope. Ask only for what you use: an application requesting everything takes longer to approve.",
 "docs.sso": "Sign in with V-ENT",
 "docs.ssoBody": "Standard authorization-code flow with PKCE. If you have integrated \"Sign in with Google\" you already know this shape. Ask a V-ENT admin to approve SSO for your partner account and you get a client id and a secret, shown once.",
 "docs.ssoScopes": "Identity scopes",
 "docs.ssoSecurity": "The code is single use and short lived, and the wrong PKCE verifier is refused. Swap it from your server, never from the browser: the client secret must not reach a page anybody can read.",
 "docs.ssoStep1": "1. Send them to V-ENT",
 "docs.ssoStep2": "2. Swap the code, on your server",
 "docs.ssoStep3": "3. Read who they are",
 "docs.step1": "Apply on the partners page, saying what you are building and which scopes you need.",
 "docs.step2": "A V-ENT admin reviews it and approves the scopes you may have. They can approve fewer than you asked for.",
 "docs.step3": "Issue a key from your partner page. The secret is shown once and never again, so store it before you close the tab.",
