 "manage.refusedHint": "Only the person running this event can open its workspace. The event page itself is open to everybody.",
 "format.gsl": "GSL Groups",
 "format.gslBlurb": "Groups of four, each playing five matches, feeding a knockout stage.",
 "format.aggregate": "Aggregate League",
 "format.aggregateBlurb": "Each fixture is several matches, one per seat, and the tie is decided on total goals rather than matches won.",
 "format.ladder": "Ladder",
 "format.ladderBlurb": "A standing table that people climb by challenging the players above them.",
 "format.noteSingle": "A field that is not a power of two needs byes in the first round, which the strongest seeds should receive.",
 "format.noteDouble": "Twice the matches of single elimination for the same field, so it needs roughly twice the time. The grand final is where organisers differ: a bracket reset gives the lower-bracket side the two wins the upper-bracket side has already earned.",
 "format.noteRoundRobin": "Matches grow with the square of the field: eight teams is 28 matches, sixteen is 120. Past about twelve it wants splitting into groups.",
 "format.noteSwiss": "Rounds are usually enough to separate the field: 5 rounds for 16, 6 for 32. Teams reaching three wins advance and three losses are out, which is the shape a Counter-Strike major runs.",
 "format.noteGsl": "Five matches per group of four: two openers, a winners match, a losers match, and a decider. It feeds a knockout stage.",
 "format.noteBattleRoyale": "The placement table is the argument: PUBG Mobile pays 10 for a win down to 1 for eighth, Free Fire pays 12 down to 1 for tenth. Both pay 1 a kill. Set it to match the game being played.",
 "format.noteAggregate": "The EA FC league format V-ENT already runs. A tie is TOTAL GOALS across the per-player fixtures, never a win count.",
 "format.noteLadder": "Good for a season that runs for weeks rather than an afternoon.",
