 "docs.failure": "Failure",
 "docs.limits": "Rate limit",
 "docs.limitsBody": "60 requests a minute per key. Ask if you need more, and say what for. Rankings and finished brackets change rarely, so a minute of caching costs you nothing and keeps you well inside it.",
 "docs.noWallet": "There is no scope that reads a wallet, a balance, a transaction, a payout or an identity document, and there will not be one. It is written into the code rather than into a policy.",
 "docs.paging": "Paging",
 "docs.pagingBody": "Every list pages the same way. page starts at 1, page_size defaults to 25 and stops at 100. Page with has_more rather than by counting: it comes from the same query as the rows, so it cannot disagree with them.",
 "docs.pkce": "Make a PKCE pair first",
 "docs.pkceBody": "Keep the verifier in the visitor session on your server; it never leaves it. Send only the challenge. If you send a challenge, that is what is checked and your client secret is not consulted, which is why a browser app never needs one.",
 "docs.readMoneyK": "Money is a decimal string",
 "docs.readMoneyV": "\"220000.00\", not a number. Parse it as a decimal. A prize pool that has been through a float is one you will eventually show wrong.",
 "docs.readPrivateK": "Only public records",
 "docs.readPrivateV": "Drafts, private tournaments and anything belonging to a suspended account are never returned, and no scope opens them.",
 "docs.readSlugK": "Address records by slug",
 "docs.readSlugV": "Every V-ENT address a person sees uses the slug, and a renamed record keeps its old addresses working. It is what you want in a link back to us.",
 "docs.readTimeK": "Times are UTC, ISO 8601",
 "docs.readTimeV": "With the Z on the end. Convert for your own readers; do not assume Lagos.",
 "docs.reading": "Four things worth knowing before you build",
 "docs.revoke": "Anybody who has signed in with V-ENT can remove the connection from their account, and existing tokens stop working. Handle BAD_TOKEN by sending them through the flow again, not by holding a dead session.",
 "docs.subK": "Key the account on sub",
 "docs.subV": "Not on the username. A person can change their username; sub is stable for the life of the account and is the only field here that is safe as a primary key on your side.",
 "docs.success": "Success",
